%div.home
  %header
    %h1
      Hi, I'm Mário, a software engineer.

  %article
    %h2
      I build web applications, front to back.

    %p
      Most of my career has been full-stack web development, from small websites to applications with intricate user experiences and complex backend architectures.
    %p
      My preferred stack is a <mark>Ruby on Rails</mark> backend with a <mark>React</mark> frontend, on top of <mark>PostgreSQL</mark>. I've written code in plenty of other languages along the way.

  %article
    %h2
      I like building infrastructure and systems.

    %p
      I've run applications on managed platforms like <mark>Amazon Web Services</mark> and <mark>Heroku</mark>, and on bare hardware with my own web servers and databases. I self-host my own services on <mark>Docker</mark> and <mark>nginx</mark>, and I build the tools I need to run them. When the trade-offs are acceptable, I prefer the simplicity of knowing exactly what's running and how.

  %article
    %h2
      I still take things apart for fun.

    %p
      This blog started with software-defined radio, Raspberry Pis and Arduinos with Nokia screens. Lately it's ESP32s: I turned a <a href="/2026/10/19/a-graphing-calculator-as-an-ssh-terminal.html">TI Voyage 200 graphing calculator into an SSH terminal</a> by reverse engineering its link port. I also put my <a href="/2026/08/27/a-live-world-map-of-my-home-routers-connections.html">home router's live connections on a world map</a>. There's more on the <a href="/blog.html">blog</a>.

  %article
    %h2
      More about me

    %p
      My detailed career and professional experience is on my <a href="{{ site.linkedin_url }}">LinkedIn</a> profile, and my personal projects are on <a href="{{ site.github_url }}">GitHub</a>. You can reach me by <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">email</a>. If you'd like to communicate securely, here's my <a href="{{ site.keybase_url }}/pgp_keys.asc?fingerprint={{ site.pgp_public_key_fingerprint}}">public key</a> (<span class="pre inline">{{ site.pgp_public_key_fingerprint | upcase}}</span>) and <a href="{{ site.keybase_url }}">Keybase</a> profile.
